course: dictionary
lesson: 3384
title: Two meanings of one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Exodus is a noun with two meanings. With a capital E, Exodus is the second book of the Bible, which tells how Moses led the Israelites out of slavery in Egypt. With a small e, an exodus is when a large number of people leave a place at the same time.
explain: «Passover, or Pesach, is a spring festival remembering the Exodus from Egypt.» The words Egypt and remembering show you that this is the Bible story. To check, swap in the meaning: remembering people leaving Egypt together makes sense here, so you have found the right one.
explain: Newspapers often use the second meaning. A mass exodus describes crowds leaving a city, or fans leaving a match early. Look for clues such as crowds, leaving and at the same time. If you see those clues, the word means a big group leaving together.
fact: Exodus is a noun, and it can mean two different things.
fact: With a capital E, Exodus is the name of the second book of the Bible.
fact: The Exodus story tells how Moses led the Israelites out of slavery in Egypt.
fact: An exodus is when a large number of people leave a place at the same time.
fact: «Passover», or Pesach, is a spring festival remembering the Exodus from Egypt; it has the Seder meal and matzah, a flat bread made without yeast.
exercise: «Passover, or Pesach, is a spring festival remembering the Exodus from Egypt.» What does Exodus mean here? | *Moses leading the Israelites out of slavery in Egypt | A spring song sung at school | A large crowd of fans leaving a football match early | A flat bread made without yeast
exercise: Newspapers say «a mass exodus» from the city. What does that mean? | *Crowds leaving a place at the same time | A book about animals | Rain falling on a hill | One person quietly sitting down
exercise: «Passover, or Pesach, is a spring festival remembering the Exodus from Egypt, with the Seder meal and matzah.» Find and copy the word that names the meal. | *Seder | matzah | Pesach | spring
test: Which of these is the book of the Bible that tells how Moses led the Israelites out of Egypt? | A book of songs for the spring festival | *Exodus | A book about animals in the desert | A book about a king who built a castle
test: Which word means a large number of people leaving a place at the same time? | Matzah | Commandment | Festival | *Exodus
exam: A news writer says «a mass exodus» from a city. Why? | Because everyone is coming into the city | Because the people are asleep | Because a new city has just been built | *Because lots of people are leaving it together
